A||||10||v8vinnie||rear air vents||||1||
Z||000000||v8vinnie||01-05-2001||07:15 PM||||hey guys, got another question for ya!.iF I REMOVE THE BOTTOM PART OF THE REAR VENTS, would it cool the rear engine compartment faster, i know it will probably get dirtier back in their, but it gets wet when it rains any way. Any one try this out,i thought i could get rid of the heat faster, and i also plan on putting on that holley scoop on the side by summer, any thoughts?||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||01-05-2001||07:54 PM||||I guess you are talking about the louvered stamped sheet under the cast grille?  I have heard of removing these for greater cooling.  Or you could replace the louvered sheet with an open mesh like '85.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-05-2001||07:58 PM||||If you have the screen with the hex shaped holes it probably won't make any dif. If you have the stamped louvers you Might get better cooling. It depends on a few things.....<P>If you do yank the stamped louvers then replace it with some kind of screen. You don't want stuff from trees etc falling in there. could start a fire. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||01-05-2001||09:37 PM||||Or better yet, replace the vents with '84 style non-vents and use a scoop (similar to Toms) to exhaust the hot air.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||01-05-2001||09:56 PM||||I took mine out. It does let the air flow through a little better but I don't know if it makes it any cooler. I should have put them back for winter because I think that ice is getting in and freezing my shifter linkage.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||01-05-2001||11:57 PM||||Good point.... I use an old style set of grates in summer and but my original with the stamped louver sheet in for winter and spring. damn maple keys.....||||reg||1
Z||000006||MrPBody||01-06-2001||11:04 AM||||. . . and pine needles, and little oak leaves.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||01-06-2001||03:14 PM||||I removed the louvered stamped sheet on mine.  Having a second set with the screen or left stock to pop in during the fall or winter is definitely a good idea.<P>I know you're probably looking for a Holley scoop, but click the link in my profile for info about a custom side scoop.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Archie||01-06-2001||08:39 PM||||On my own cars, I take them out all the time.<P>If it keeps the engine compartment cooler that's ok by me, but I take them out so that passers-by can see a glint of Chrome or a K/N Filter or what have you as they pass by.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||01-08-2001||05:44 AM||||I took those out of my GT a while ago.  Does tend to let a bit more leaves and stuff down there, but not so much that it creates a problem.  Haven't had any issues with snow down there, either.  The design of the vent's seems to block most of the snow from getting under them.||||reg||
Z||000010||v8vinnie||01-08-2001||08:25 PM||||thanks for the opinions guys, have no snow here in florida ,just sunshine,||||reg||1
